From 95c06741aa230767b18865c7f0ba49f40d29a8fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Braden <snufflyy@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 00:05:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] spurs: real PPU side of SPURS Queue (PopBody/PushBody,
 attach/detach) and LFQueue init

cellSpursQueuePopBody had no handler at all, so the dispatcher's faked
CELL_OK read as "popped" with nothing written, and _cellSpursQueueInitialize
wrote its own layout (size at +0x10, buffer at +0x18), which the task side of
the queue does not use.

The other end of a SPURS queue is task code linked from libspurs, working on
the 128-byte queue line in guest memory with GETLLAR/PUTLLC, so the line is
the interface. Its layout and protocol are derived from that task code's own
reads and writes (push begin/end in a title's SPU images): pop/push ring
indices at +0x00/+0x04 over [0, 2*depth), ~index while a side is in progress;
size +0x08, depth +0x0C, buffer u64 +0x10, SPU event port +0x18 (-1 none),
direction +0x1C; push/pop waiter task lists at +0x20/+0x30 with workload ids
at +0x40/+0x50; taskset u64 +0x60. A side that frees room or adds an item
hands the in-progress mark to the head waiter and signals it.

New libs/spurs/cellSpursQueue.c:
- _cellSpursQueueInitialize writes that line (argument checks as libsre).
- cellSpursQueuePopBody(queue, buf, isPeek, isBlocking) and
  cellSpursQueuePushBody(queue, buf, isBlocking) built on four queue-pointer
  primitives (get/complete push/pop pointer), each one atomic transaction under
  the lock-line lock with the SPU reservation invalidated; errors are the real
  CELL_SPURS_TASK_ERROR values (AGAIN 0x80410901, BUSY 0x8041090A, ...), which
  titles compare against (cellSpurs.h's TASK_ERROR macros are 0x804107xx).
- Blocking calls retry non-blocking tries and sleep until an SPU commits the
  queue line (the SPU line-commit hook, now dispatched to event flags and
  queues alike) or a PPU push/pop completes, with a 1 ms timeout.
- cellSpursQueueAttach/DetachLv2EventQueue create an lv2 queue, bind a SPURS
  SPU port (cellSpursAttachLv2EventQueue's binding, refactored into
  spurs_bind_event_port) and publish it at +0x18.
- cellSpursQueueClear empties an idle queue.
- _cellSpursLFQueueInitialize: libsre's line, write for write.

Ported from soyjxck/dod3-recomp src/kernel/spurs_queue.cpp and
src/kernel/spurs_lfqueue.cpp (MIT): the entry-point ABI, the blocking
retry/wake structure and the LFQueue initializer. dod3 runs Sony's lifted
libsre for the pointer primitives; those are written here from the task-side
code instead, so no firmware is needed.

tests/test_spurs_queue.c (ctest spurs_queue on POSIX) round-trips the PPU HLE
against a C model of the task-side push on the real big-endian line: layout,
wrap past 2*depth, peek, AGAIN when empty/full, a blocked task push woken by a
PPU pop, PPU push waking a parked popper, direction checks, attach/detach, and
12,000 items from 3 producer threads through a depth-8 queue in FIFO order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
